  "term": "fetal distress",
  "definition": "Fetal distress is a term used when signs during labor suggest the fetus may not be getting enough oxygen. In the packet, it refers to a diagnosis often based on interpreting cardiotocograph patterns, sometimes with added technologies to confirm suspected fetal hypoxia.",
